overflow in sub at i64

The length axis of the trapping set. `i64::MIN + 2` does NOT trap on a
two-element series -- `tests/rolling.ch` asserts it returns `[None, None]` --
but it DOES trap on a three-element one, because the largest index is 2 and
`2 - (i64::MIN + 2)` overflows.

Without this case every pin on the trapping set would hold the series length at
2, and an implementation with a fixed trapping set of `{i64::MIN, i64::MIN + 1}`
would satisfy all of them while the documented claim says the set scales with
`len(xs)`.
